          "A person already baptized does not repeat the sacrament. The promises can be repeated, and the Church loves to repeat them here and at the Easter Vigil. Parents can tell children the date of their baptism on this Sunday and set out the candle or the garment if it has been kept. Adults who cannot find the record can still ask a parish to help, using the [[/blog/how-to-find-catholic-church-near-me/|parish guide]]. Those preparing for baptism at Easter have a patron feast in January. The [[/blog/catholic-baptism-preparation-guide/|preparation guide]] and the [[/blog/catholic-confirmation-guide/|confirmation guide]] belong beside it, because the Spirit who descended on the Son is the Spirit given in confirmation.",
