          "He was a publisher because the streets were full of cheap print that mocked the Church. The Catholic Readings, his pamphlet series, gave ordinary people something true at a price they could pay. Patronage of editors and of Catholic teachers grew from that labor, and it is a sound popular instinct. It is patronage by resemblance, the sort the [[/blog/patron-saints-guide/|patron saints guide]] describes, rather than a claim that every editorial decision now has a heavenly guarantee. Print the truth, teach a trade, hear a confession, stay in the yard.",
